Inboard and Outboard Bearings

The image included with this post is the simplest way of showing inboard vs outboard for a motor and pump.

Why it matters: Understanding basic rotating equipment terms helps to troubleshoot and communicate about issues. When a mechanic tells you there is an issue with the motor outboard bearing, it helps to be able to picture it in your mind right away.

- Bearings maintain the position of the rotating shaft.
- They must be able to absorb forces to prevent misalignment.
- Forces can be radial or axial.
- Radial: Perpendicular to shaft
- Axial (Thrust): Parallel to shaft

